      "id": 1,
      "text": "When the Chicago, Rock Island and Pacific Railroad arrived in 1869, Underwood sprang up three miles northeast of abandoned Downsville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwood%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The principal early settlers of the area arrived during the period from 1845 to 1850.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwood%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1847, a flour mill and a saw mill were built on Mosquito Creek; the flour mill was destroyed by a flood in 1850.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwood%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first school was built in 1863, and soon more homes were built near the school and saw mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwood%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The name Underwood comes from the first engineer to run a train over the Milwaukee tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwood%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "From 1907 to 1910 the telephone came to town, a water works system was installed and cement sidewalks constructed.",
